.TH tucsv n 0.2 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tucsv
.PP
Small CSV helpers written in pure Tcl.
.PP
\fBtuCSV\fR handles common CSV tasks:
.IP \(bu
parse one CSV line into a Tcl list
.IP \(bu
join a Tcl list into one CSV line
.IP \(bu
parse CSV text into rows
.IP \(bu
read/write CSV files
.IP \(bu
convert rows into dictionaries using a header row
.PP
It is intentionally small and dependency\-free. It is not intended to replace a full CSV/database import framework.
.SS Load
.CS
tcl::tm::path add /path/to/tclutils/lib/tm
package require tclutils::tucsv
.CE
.SS "Parse one line"
.CS
set row [::tclutils::tucsv::parseLine {a,"b,c","d""e"}]
# -> a {b,c} {d"e}
.CE
.PP
Options:
.CS
-delimiter ,
-quote "
-trim 0
.CE
.SS "Join one line"
.CS
set line [::tclutils::tucsv::joinLine [list a {b,c} {d"e}]]
# -> a,"b,c","d""e"
.CE
.PP
Options:
.CS
-delimiter ,
-quote "
-alwaysQuote 0
.CE
.SS "Parse text"
.CS
set rows [::tclutils::tucsv::parse "name,city\nAlice,Berlin"]
# -> {name city} {Alice Berlin}
.CE
.PP
Quoted fields may contain newlines.
.SS "Convert rows to dicts"
.CS
set rows [::tclutils::tucsv::parse "name;city\nAlice;Berlin" -delimiter {;}]
set dictRows [::tclutils::tucsv::dicts $rows]
# -> {name Alice city Berlin}
.CE
.SS Files
.CS
set rows [::tclutils::tucsv::file data.csv -delimiter {;}]
::tclutils::tucsv::writeFile out.csv $rows
::tclutils::tucsv::writeFile out.csv $rows -profile excel-de
.CE
.PP
\fBfile\fR and \fBwriteFile\fR take \fB\-encoding\fR (default \fButf\-8\fR). \fBwriteFile\fR writes the line ends given by \fB\-newline\fR unchanged; without it the platform default applies. It writes through a temporary file (\fBcommon::replaceFile\fR): a failed write leaves the old file and no open channel (tclutils 0.69.0).
.SS Profiles
.PP
\fB\-profile\fR works with \fBtext\fR, \fBfile\fR and \fBwriteFile\fR. Options given after it override its values.
.TS
l l.
Profile	Sets
\fBexcel\-de\fR	\fB\-delimiter ;\fR, \fB\-newline \er\en\fR, \fB\-bom 1\fR
\fBrfc4180\fR	\fB\-delimiter ,\fR, \fB\-newline \er\en\fR
.TE
.PP
\fB\-bom 1\fR puts a UTF\-8 byte order mark in front of the text, so Excel opens the file as UTF\-8. An unknown profile raises \fB{TCLUTILS TUCSV PROFILE <name>}\fR.
.SS "Options (0.37.0)"
.IP \(bu
A leading UTF\-8 BOM is stripped automatically on \fBparse\fR.
.IP \(bu
\fB\-strict 0\fR recovers from an unterminated quoted field instead of raising \fB{TCLUTILS TUCSV QUOTE}\fR (useful for loading messy real\-world exports). The default \fB\-strict 1\fR keeps the previous strict behaviour.
.SS "Additional exported commands"
.PP
Documented for completeness (same module, also covered by the test suite):
.CS
tucsv::text rows args                          ;# format ROWS (a list of field lists) as CSV text; -delimiter -quote -alwaysQuote -newline -bom -profile
.CE
